    "locked": false,
    "maintainer_can_modify": true,
    "title": "descriptor: Represent multipath descriptors in a single Descriptor object",
    "user": {
      "login": "achow101",
      "id": 3782274,
      "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjM3ODIyNzQ=",
      "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3782274?v=4",
      "gravatar_id": "",
      "url": "https://api.github.com/users/achow101",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/achow101",
      "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/achow101/followers",
      "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/achow101/following%7B/other_user%7D",
      "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/achow101/gists%7B/gist_id%7D",
      "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/achow101/starred%7B/owner%7D%7B/repo%7D",
      "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/achow101/subscriptions",
      "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/achow101/orgs",
      "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/achow101/repos",
      "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/achow101/events%7B/privacy%7D",
      "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/achow101/received_events",
      "type": "User",
      "site_admin": false,
      "name": null,
      "patch_url": null
    },
    "body": "Currently, multipath descriptor strings treat the multipath specifiers as syntactic sugar. Once we finish parsing such a string, the multipath elements are lost as the result is the multiple distinct descriptors that the multipath is a shorthand for. This means that we are unable to return the multipath string for such descriptors.\r\n\r\nThis PR allows descriptors to actually be multipath where the multipath specifiers are represented inside of the paths of `BIP32PubkeyProvider`s. This allows for the multipath string to be produced.\r\n\r\nIn order to achieve this, a lot of derivation path parsing is refactored. `KeyPath` is promoted to being its own class (which subclasses `std::vector`), while the individual derivation indexes become a `KeyPathElement` object so that the multipath elements can be represented. Furthermore, hardened derivation characters are now being stored within `KeyPathElement`s so each element knows what the original hardened character was. This also cleans up a little bit of the descriptor implementation as we no longer have to carry around `bool apostrophe` in a bunch of places.\r\n\r\nLastly, `Parse` now returns a single `Descriptor` object, rather than a vector of them. If the descriptor is a multipath descriptor, the expansion can be retrieved using `GetMultipathExpansion()`. The wallet uses this and still must not store multipath descriptors. ",
